    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0371" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54Guat/pg341"/>

                <head>195. Memorandum of Telephone Conversation Between the Assistant Secretary of
                    State for Inter-American Affairs (Holland) and Secretary of State Dulles<anchor n="1" xml:id="d195-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-06-17T17:15:00-04:00">June
                        17, 1954, 5:15 p.m.</date></dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">TELEPHONE CALL FROM MR. HOLLAND</p>
                <p>He said Sec. Anderson just told him that he has a military
                    telegram from Honduras that Armas(?) “is moving’. The Sec. said he didn’t know
                    what that means, but he supposes it means something. H. said A. is a
                    revolutionary individual lurking in the forest.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
